 {:name "spread-small-pairwise-correlations-across-growing-triangular-support"
  :lane :solve-lane
  :level :counterexample-construction
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:target-class
   "Refute a uniform-constant approximation estimate inferred only from small pairwise correlations."
   :construction
   {:ambient-space "`ℓ²(ℕ)` with coordinate basis `e_i`"
    :coefficients
    ["`a_m = 2^(-(m+1))`"
     "`b_m = sqrt(1 - m * a_m^2)`"]
    :vectors
    "`f_m = a_m * ∑_{i<m} e_i + b_m * e_m`"}
   :checks
   [{:property :unit-norm
     :calculation "`‖f_m‖² = m*a_m² + b_m² = 1`"}
    {:property :pairwise-hypothesis
     :calculation
     "For `n < m`, `|⟪f_n,f_m⟫| = a_m * (n*a_n + b_n) ≤ (3/2)*a_m ≤ 2^(-m)`."}
    {:property :gram-schmidt-output
     :calculation
     "The family is triangular with positive diagonal, so normalized Gram–Schmidt returns the coordinate basis vector `e_m` at stage `m`."}
    {:property :aggregate-error
     :calculation
     "`‖f_m - e_m‖ ≥ sqrt(m)*a_m = (sqrt(m)/2)*2^(-m)`."}]
   :contradiction
   "A bound `‖f_m-e_m‖ ≤ C*2^(-m)` would force `C ≥ sqrt(m)/2` for every `m`, so no uniform constant exists."
   :transferable-shape
   "Distribute individually small off-diagonal coefficients over `m` earlier coordinates. The per-pair hypothesis remains small, while their aggregate `ℓ²` mass grows by a `sqrt(m)` factor."
   :boundary
   "The construction proves that any valid conclusion must permit at least the displayed `sqrt(m)` loss or impose stronger aggregate correlation control. It does not prove that a particular `C*sqrt(m)*2^(-m)` upper bound is sufficient."
   :rule
   "To test a uniform-constant claim derived from pairwise bounds, build a triangular family whose support grows with the index; compare the pairwise scale with the square-summed aggregate scale before attempting the proof."
   :capture-kind :runner-counterexample-and-ground-control-checked-asymptotics}
